Z||000001||Nashco||06-02-2001||01:00 PM||||I have a 69 bug and an 88 GT (check out my profile for a link).  I love my bug, and it's awesome in the dunes and dirt roads, but it just doesn't compare to the GT.  Yes, convertible is nice, yes, it is the easiest car in the world to work on, and yes, parts are about 20% the price and easier to get.  BUT, the bug was one of those cars you have to replace everything on it to get it reliable.  I replaced basically everything (rebuilt engine, replaced tranny, rebuilt front end, all new bearings and brakes, motor and trans mounts, lots of wiring and electrical parts, fuel tank, light lenses, etc.) over the course of about two years...you have to work on it every weekend whether you want to or not.  Sometimes it's nice to take a break, or upgrade only when you want to.<P>It's nice that your bro loves his bug...but after he gets something that's not stock he'll realize what an ass he was being.  Even on a dirt road my GT would whip my bug's ass if the bug was still stock....straightaways I'd blow past the bug.  The bug is fun, but not a supercar.  I have done lots of mods to mine, and I'm still doing lots, because I want it to be as fast as a sports car and still have the bug driving characteristics.<P>Tell your brother to have an open mind about things, to grow up, and to experience more than just a stock VW.  Headers, 2 bbl Weber, and a Mallory dual-point distributor really woke up my 1600 dual port...time and money...not talk..made it better.  Oh, and tell him to research and learn more about the car, rather than talking it up for no reason.<P>I don't mind him being on the forum, but I do mind him being an ass.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
